{"id": "Derp3Ejx_49", "title": "Video by therishikatha", "description": "Why is Krishna called DAMODAR? 🪢 His mom tried to tie him up… and the rope was ALWAYS two fingers short.\n\nMaa Yashoda was churning butter when little Kanha came asking for his milk. She scooped him up, but the milk on the stove boiled over and she ran to save it. Left alone, Kanha got cross… and SMASHED the curd pot with a stone! 😱\n\nMaa came back to a broken pot and found him sitting on an upside-down mortar, feeding the butter to the monkeys. 🐒 She picked up a stick. Kanha RAN. Even yogis can't catch him in meditation… but Maa did!\n\nHe cried and rubbed his eyes till his kajal was everywhere. So Maa threw the stick away and decided to tie him to the mortar instead. The rope was two fingers short. She tied on another rope: still two fingers short. Every rope in the house: STILL two fingers! The neighbours laughed, and Maa was tired and sweating, flowers falling from her hair.\n\nSeeing his mother so tired, Kanha let her tie him up. 💛 That's why he's Damodar: the one with a rope (dama) round his belly (udara). Then he dragged the mortar between two arjuna trees, they crashed down, and out stepped two devas, freed from Narad Muni's curse! (Srimad Bhagavatam 10.9–10.10)\n\n📚 Want more stories like this for your little ones? Rishi Katha picture books: Books 1–3, set of 3 for ₹500 at rishikatha.com (link in bio).\n\n💬 Is anyone in YOUR family named Damodar? Tag them below 👇\n❤️ Save this for Kartik month and share it with every mom who's chased a toddler.\n➡️ Follow @therishikatha: in Part 3, Narad Muni visits Krishna's 16,108 palaces… and finds him in every one.\n\n#krishna #damodar #damodarlila #kanha #yashoda #balkrishna #kartikmonth #damodarashtakam #krishnaleela #bhagavatam #harekrishna #littlekrishna #indianmythology #storiesforkids #rishikatha", "channel": "therishikatha", "uploader_id": "22569163881", "uploader": "Rishi Katha", "timestamp": 1792426331, "like_count": 12112, "comment_coun